{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794313956076,"sessionID":"ses_e3a9bc48effe0IpMJNFD0aHrVw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Atgk3YSrxTjG6yaOWbbssxeq","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json\n@@\n     \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n+    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/src/Modal.tsx\n@@\n-  const [registered, setRegistered] = useState(false);\n   const submit = async (event: FormEvent) => {\n     event.preventDefault(); setBusy(true); setError(\"\");\n+    let registered = false;\n@@\n-        setRegistered(true);\n+        registered = true;\n*** Update File: /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@\n-        value = json_body().get(\"value\")\n+        raw_value = json_body().get(\"value\")\n         try:\n-            valid = type(value) in (int, float) and math.isfinite(value)\n+            value = float(raw_value) if type(raw_value) in (int, float) else None\n+            valid = value is not None and math.isfinite(value)\n*** Update File: /workspace/.dockerignore\n@@\n-data/*.db\n-data/*.sqlite\n-data/*.sqlite3\n+data\n*** Update File: /workspace/README.md\n@@\n-# App\n+# Fieldwork — Sensor dashboard\n@@\n Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\n+.venv/bin/python backend/app.py\n+```\n+\n+In another terminal:\n+\n+```sh\n+cd frontend\n+npm ci\n+npm run dev\n+```\n+\n+Vite proxies `/api` to the backend on port 8000. To serve everything from Flask, run `npm run build` in `frontend/`, then start the backend. Sensor pages support direct navigation at `/sensors/{id}`.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+```sh\n+.venv/bin/python -m unittest backend.test_app -v\n+cd frontend\n+npm run lint\n+npm run typecheck\n+npm run build\n+```\n+\n+## Accounts and data\n+\n+Register with `POST /api/auth/register`, then sign in with `POST /api/auth/login`. Both accept `username` and `password`. Login returns an opaque bearer token valid for 30 days; use `Authorization: Bearer <token>` for write requests. `GET /api/auth/me` identifies the current account and `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes its token. Passwords are hashed, and only hashed tokens are stored.\n+\n+SQLite is stored at `./data/sensors.sqlite3`. Set `DATABASE_PATH` to override its location. Mount `/app/data` in the container to retain users, sessions, sensors, and readings across container replacement. Sensors are public; only their owner can add readings or delete them. Reading values must be finite numbers; history supports `limit` from 1 to 1000 (default 100), newest first. Timestamps are server-generated UTC values.\n+\n+The frontend refreshes every 10 seconds. An empty public workspace displays clearly labeled illustrative demo sensors; these are not persisted and disappear when real sensors are registered or a user signs in.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM frontend/tsconfig.json\nM frontend/src/Modal.tsx\nM backend/app.py\nM .dockerignore\nM README.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json\n+++ /workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json\n@@ -4,8 +4,9 @@\n \"lib\": [\"ES2022\", \"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\"],\n \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n+\"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n \"strict\": true,\n \"noEmit\": true,\n \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n\nIndex: /workspace/frontend/src/Modal.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/Modal.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/Modal.tsx\n@@ -49,16 +49,16 @@\n const [username, setUsername] = useState(\"\");\n const [password, setPassword] = useState(\"\");\n const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false);\n const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n-const [registered, setRegistered] = useState(false);\n const submit = async (event: FormEvent) => {\n   event.preventDefault(); setBusy(true); setError(\"\");\n+  let registered = false;\n   try {\n     const credentials = { username: username.trim(), password };\n     if (mode === \"register\") {\n       await api(\"/auth/register\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify(credentials) });\n-      setRegistered(true);\n+      registered = true;\n     }\n     const response = await api<{ token: string }>(\"/auth/login\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify(credentials) });\n     onLogin({ token: response.token, username: credentials.username });\n   } catch (exception) { setError(exception instanceof Error ? exception.message : \"Unable to sign in.\"); if (registered) setMode(\"login\"); }\n\nIndex: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -260,11 +260,12 @@\n @application.post(\"/api/sensors/<int:sensor_id>/readings\")\n @authenticated\n def add_reading(sensor_id):\n     find_sensor(sensor_id, owned=True)\n-    value = json_body().get(\"value\")\n+    raw_value = json_body().get(\"value\")\n     try:\n-        valid = type(value) in (int, float) and math.isfinite(value)\n+        value = float(raw_value) if type(raw_value) in (int, float) else None\n+        valid = value is not None and math.isfinite(value)\n     except OverflowError:\n         valid = False\n     if not valid:\n         raise ApiError(\"value must be a finite number.\", 400)\n\nIndex: /workspace/.dockerignore\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/.dockerignore\n+++ /workspace/.dockerignore\n@@ -4,7 +4,5 @@\n **/__pycache__\n **/*.pyc\n **/.git\n frontend/dist\n-data/*.db\n-data/*.sqlite\n-data/*.sqlite3\n+data\n\nIndex: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n-# App\n+# Fieldwork — Sensor dashboard\n \n ## Run contract\n \n - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n@@ -12,4 +12,40 @@\n - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n \n Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\n+.venv/bin/python backend/app.py\n+```\n+\n+In another terminal:\n+\n+```sh\n+cd frontend\n+npm ci\n+npm run dev\n+```\n+\n+Vite proxies `/api` to the backend on port 8000. To serve everything from Flask, run `npm run build` in `frontend/`, then start the backend. Sensor pages support direct navigation at `/sensors/{id}`.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+```sh\n+.venv/bin/python -m unittest backend.test_app -v\n+cd frontend\n+npm run lint\n+npm run typecheck\n+npm run build\n+```\n+\n+## Accounts and data\n+\n+Register with `POST /api/auth/register`, then sign in with `POST /api/auth/login`. Both accept `username` and `password`. Login returns an opaque bearer token valid for 30 days; use `Authorization: Bearer <token>` for write requests. `GET /api/auth/me` identifies the current account and `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes its token. Passwords are hashed, and only hashed tokens are stored.\n+\n+SQLite is stored at `./data/sensors.sqlite3`. Set `DATABASE_PATH` to override its location. Mount `/app/data` in the container to retain users, sessions, sensors, and readings across container replacement. Sensors are public; only their owner can add readings or delete them. Reading values must be finite numbers; history supports `limit` from 1 to 1000 (default 100), newest first. Timestamps are server-generated UTC values.\n+\n+The frontend refreshes every 10 seconds. An empty public workspace displays clearly labeled illustrative demo sensors; these are not persisted and disappear when real sensors are registered or a user signs in.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json","relativePath":"frontend/tsconfig.json","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json\n+++ /workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json\n@@ -4,8 +4,9 @@\n \"lib\": [\"ES2022\", \"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\"],\n \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n+\"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n \"strict\": true,\n \"noEmit\": true,\n \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n","additions":1,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/Modal.tsx","relativePath":"frontend/src/Modal.tsx","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/Modal.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/Modal.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/Modal.tsx\n@@ -49,16 +49,16 @@\n const [username, setUsername] = useState(\"\");\n const [password, setPassword] = useState(\"\");\n const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false);\n const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n-const [registered, setRegistered] = useState(false);\n const submit = async (event: FormEvent) => {\n   event.preventDefault(); setBusy(true); setError(\"\");\n+  let registered = false;\n   try {\n     const credentials = { username: username.trim(), password };\n     if (mode === \"register\") {\n       await api(\"/auth/register\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify(credentials) });\n-      setRegistered(true);\n+      registered = true;\n     }\n     const response = await api<{ token: string }>(\"/auth/login\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify(credentials) });\n     onLogin({ token: response.token, username: credentials.username });\n   } catch (exception) { setError(exception instanceof Error ? exception.message : \"Unable to sign in.\"); if (registered) setMode(\"login\"); }\n","additions":2,"deletions":2},{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py","relativePath":"backend/app.py","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -260,11 +260,12 @@\n @application.post(\"/api/sensors/<int:sensor_id>/readings\")\n @authenticated\n def add_reading(sensor_id):\n     find_sensor(sensor_id, owned=True)\n-    value = json_body().get(\"value\")\n+    raw_value = json_body().get(\"value\")\n     try:\n-        valid = type(value) in (int, float) and math.isfinite(value)\n+        value = float(raw_value) if type(raw_value) in (int, float) else None\n+        valid = value is not None and math.isfinite(value)\n     except OverflowError:\n         valid = False\n     if not valid:\n         raise ApiError(\"value must be a finite number.\", 400)\n","additions":3,"deletions":2},{"filePath":"/workspace/.dockerignore","relativePath":".dockerignore","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/.dockerignore\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/.dockerignore\n+++ /workspace/.dockerignore\n@@ -4,7 +4,5 @@\n **/__pycache__\n **/*.pyc\n **/.git\n frontend/dist\n-data/*.db\n-data/*.sqlite\n-data/*.sqlite3\n+data\n","add